---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { profile } from '../../data/profile';
---
<Base lang="en" title={`Resume — ${profile.name}`} description="Resume of Miguel Antonio Quevedo Simoza: Multiplatform Software Engineer (Desktop, Mobile, Web), Flutter, Rust, Unity C#, Next.js, SQL/NoSQL & AI.">
  <main id="contenido" class="detail-main wrap">
    <a class="back-link" href="/en/">← Back to portfolio</a>
    <div class="cv-actions">
      <button class="button button-primary" type="button" onclick="window.print()">Print / Save PDF ↗</button>
      <a class="button button-outline" href="/cv/">Versión en español (ES) ↗</a>
    </div>
    <article class="cv-sheet">
      <h1>{profile.name}</h1>
      <p class="cv-role">Multiplatform Software Engineer (Desktop · Mobile · Web) | Flutter · Dart · Rust · Unity (C#) · Web</p>
      <p class="cv-meta">
        Estado Aragua, Venezuela (Remote · Hybrid · On-site · Full/Part-time · Open to relocate) ·
        <a href={`mailto:${profile.email}`}>{profile.email}</a> ·
        <a href={profile.linkedin} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">linkedin.com/in/miguel-quevedo-dev</a> ·
        <a href={profile.github} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">github.com/M4QSZ</a>
      </p>

      <section>
        <h2>Summary</h2>
        <p>
          End-to-end multiplatform software engineer taking concepts from 0-to-1 ideation and feedback-validated MVPs to working desktop,
          mobile and web products with 1:1 "on-model" design fidelity, modular clean architecture, offline-first persistence, native Rust
          systems, Flutter apps, Unity (C#) games and web platforms. Final-year Systems Engineering (Programming Concentration) student
          at Universidad Bicentenaria de Aragua (expected graduation: July 2027).
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Experience &amp; flagship ecosystem</h2>
        <h3>Lead Architect &amp; Multiplatform Software Engineer — Meson (Independent Product Suite)</h3>
        <p class="cv-sub">September 2025 – Present · Remote (Windows/Desktop, Mobile &amp; Web · 769/860 active-branch commits · 912,888 Dart + 50,270 Rust LOC in <code>meson_business</code>)</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>POS, Dual Self-Checkout &amp; Peripherals (<code>meson_business</code> · 2,521 Dart files / 527 test files):</strong> architected hospitality &amp; retail POS, Kitchen/Bar KDS, Restaurant &amp; Supermarket self-checkout (<code>auto_pago</code> / RS-232 &amp; USB weigh-scale anti-theft check), Flame 2.5D CAD floor planner (+70 360° isometric assets), 18 industry suites in MesOn Store and <code>device_hub</code> (CFDs, ESC/POS LAN/USB/BLE printers, NFC/RFID).</li>
          <li><strong>Industrial ERP, WebRTC Chat &amp; Atelier HR:</strong> built double-entry ledger, recipe BOM manufacturing, 3-way AP invoice matching, SENIAT fiscal hash audit, B2B supplier marketplace (80 files), WhatsApp-style chat (WebRTC VoIP/video, waveforms, screen share, QR multi-device link), Atelier talent/payroll ERP, PIN attendance kiosk and layered desktop shell (176 files, WebView2, 7-mode shrinkage/par calculator).</li>
          <li><strong>49 Rust FFI APIs &amp; 8 Crates (50,270 Rust LOC via <code>flutter_rust_bridge</code>):</strong> DAG dependency spreadsheet + XLSX engine (<code>meson_tools</code>), offline local Whisper STT fallback + Rust TTS cache &amp; SQLite TF-IDF/RAG (<code>meson_ai</code>), <code>qbsdiff</code> binary delta updater, SIMD media, hardware-bound HMAC licenses, HLC/CRDT + WAL AES-256-GCM LAN P2P, Flutter Deferred Components, adaptive cache profiles and Win32 <code>user32.dll</code> input-freeze recovery.</li>
          <li><strong>Companion Apps &amp; Web Platform:</strong> architected super-admin financial/license plane <code>meson_central</code>, offline peer-mesh courier app <code>meson_delivery</code>, social Radar app <code>meson_customer</code> (Rust backend), <code>meson_pause</code> (15 tests), <code>meson_currency</code>, public <code>BUCO</code> (22 tests), 10 decoupled packages and 189-page mobile-first Astro web platform.</li>
          <li><strong>Leadership &amp; Collaboration:</strong> solo author of Rust engines, HLC/CRDT P2P sync, NoSQL ↔ SQL migration (Firebase → Supabase/PostgreSQL) and <code>meson_central</code>; supervised one collaborator contributing Flutter UI screens (~10.6% of commits).</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Games, web & applied AI</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Brasas (Flutter & Unity C#):</strong> Shared Flutter game package (<code>meson_brasas</code> inside multiplatform Meson Pausa) plus a dedicated Unity 6.3 LTS (C#) implementation with decoupled simulation, EditMode/PlayMode tests and Python tooling.</li>
          <li><strong>El Pueblo del Faro (Roblox Studio):</strong> Independent Roblox experience in progress using client/server Luau, Rojo config and Python packaging/verification tools (Studio playtest pending).</li>
          <li><strong>Alma (Next.js) & Astro sites:</strong> Marketplace-style e-commerce storefront Alma built with Next.js, React, TypeScript and Supabase (catalog, Fuse.js search, auth, roles, admin panel, Recharts, Resend, demo checkout) plus two Astro sites (services site & QR/NFC prototype).</li>
          <li><strong>Meson IA & prototypes:</strong> Self-directed LLM integration and applied AI tooling (Meson IA), alongside a Rust Bevy 2D prototype.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Open-source crates &amp; live deployments</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong><a href="https://github.com/M4QSZ/lan-delta-sync" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">lan-delta-sync</a> (Rust · Green CI):</strong> Clean-room crate implementing Hybrid Logical Clocks, LWW CRDT convergence, anti-replay <code>ChaCha20-Poly1305</code> framing and bounded retry outbox (7 integration tests on Ubuntu &amp; Windows).</li>
          <li><strong><a href="https://github.com/M4QSZ/ffi-arena-bridge" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">ffi-arena-bridge</a> (Rust + C99 + <code>dart:ffi</code> · Green CI):</strong> Panic-safe FFI bridge featuring <code>u64</code> generational handles, <code>catch_unwind</code> boundary guard, double-free-safe buffers and live C99 <code>cdylib</code> consumer test.</li>
          <li><strong><a href="https://github.com/M4QSZ/dart-offline-outbox" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">dart-offline-outbox</a> (Dart · Green CI):</strong> Pure-Dart offline-first transactional outbox with per-entity write coalescing, jittered exponential backoff, partial batch ACKs and deterministic quarantine.</li>
          <li><strong>Public Vercel deployments:</strong> <a href="https://set-ingenieria.vercel.app" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">SET Engineering</a> (Astro + Tailwind CSS) and <a href="https://pulsera-medica.vercel.app" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">MedPulse SOS</a> (Astro + TypeScript + Supabase).</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Skills & engineering practices</h2>
        <p><strong>Core active stack:</strong> Flutter (Impeller / Skia / Deferred Components), Dart, Flame, Rust, <code>C-ABI</code> / <code>dart:ffi</code>, WebRTC, HLC / CRDTs, AES-256-GCM / Argon2, C#, Unity, Kotlin, TypeScript, JavaScript, HTML, CSS, Next.js, React, Astro, Python, Luau/Lua, PostgreSQL, Supabase, MySQL, SQLite, Cloud Firestore, Firebase, Isar, Git, Git LFS, CI/CD (GitHub Actions), Whisper STT / Local RAG AI, <code>qbsdiff</code> Binary Diffing, Win32 Interop, RS-232 / ESC-POS Hardware, Technical SEO.</p>
        <p><strong>Engineering practices:</strong> MVP architecture & feedback iteration, 1:1 "on-model" design-to-code fidelity, AI prompt optimization & current LLM criteria, Modular / Clean Architecture, Offline-First systems, NoSQL ↔ SQL migration, Automated Testing, Crash & Memory Profiling, security hardening, cross-functional team coordination & delegation, Godot, and foundational systems in C, C++, Java, PHP, Laravel and Django.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Education & languages</h2>
        <p><strong>Universidad Bicentenaria de Aragua (UBA)</strong> — B.S. in Systems Engineering, Programming Concentration (2023 – July 2027, expected).</p>
        <p><strong>Languages:</strong> Spanish (Native) · English (Bilingual / C2) · Portuguese (Advanced) · Italian (Advanced) · German (Basic) · Japanese (Basic).</p>
      </section>
    </article>
  </main>
</Base>
